# {{PROJECT_NAME}} agent guide

## Read order

1. Read `SPEC.md` for supported behavior and non-regression boundaries.
2. Read `TODO.md` for current work only.
3. Read `.learnings/ERRORS.md` before implementation. Retain it in source handoff; never use it as product input.
4. Read the relevant `research/` file before changing a research-derived behavior.
5. Read `benchmarks/README.md` before changing defaults, benchmark code, raw data or charts.
6. Read `CHANGELOG.md` before changing a public contract.

## Source map

| Path | Role |
|---|---|
| `SPEC.md` | one active product specification |
| `TODO.md` | one active backlog |
| `schema/` | generated public schemas/contracts |
| `research/` | retained source-backed research |
| `benchmarks/` | raw benchmark data and reproducible charts |
| `tools/` | tested repository automation |
| `.learnings/` | retained agent memory, never product input |

## Required loop

1. Find the exact task in `TODO.md` or contract in `SPEC.md`.
2. Inventory the behavior that must not regress.
3. Write and run a failing test before production code.
4. Implement the smallest change, then rerun the focused test.
5. Run the project task runner before handoff.
6. Update schema, benchmark, changelog or README only when their public contract changed.

## Handoff boundary

Include source, specification, research, benchmark raw data/charts and `.learnings/`. Exclude rebuildable build/cache/package artifacts. Never describe an unavailable command or unreviewed dataset as implemented.
